{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md | sed -n '49,85p;154,162p'\"","aggregated_output":"    49\t### `test/capture/converter.test.ts`\n    50\t\n    51\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n    52\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n    53\t| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\n    54\t| TC-2.8 *(risk: atomicity)* | Malformed→gap vs store-unavailable→health signal | (a) malformed on writable thread; (b) unavailable store | (a) durable queryable gap; (b) extension health signal in `SessionState.health`, no gap, no hook exception |\n    55\t| TC-2.9 | Model/thinking changes captured as ordered runtime_notes | fire `model_select` then `thinking_level_select` mid-sequence | each records one `runtime_note` carrying new+previous value; order preserved relative to surrounding messages |\n    56\t\n    57\t### `test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts`\n    58\t\n    59\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n    60\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n    61\t| TC-2.2 | One-prompt-two-tools-then-answer → exactly one LHC turn, `turn_end` at agent_end | the Flow 2 worked-example corpus | exactly one `turn_end`; emitted at `agent_end`; per-step PI `turn_end`s produce none |\n    62\t| TC-2.3 | Session order from converter source-event order, not turnIndex | two agent runs each starting turnIndex 0 | turns ordered by source-event order through the converter; no collision from repeated turnIndex 0 |\n    63\t\n    64\t### `test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts`\n    65\t\n    66\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n    67\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n    68\t| TC-2.4 | Parallel tool calls, out-of-order completion, correlate by id | assistant with toolCalls a,b; results arrive b,a | each `tool_result` correlated to its call by `toolCallId`, not arrival order |\n    69\t| TC-2.5 | Error tool result captured with flag + content | toolResult `isError:true` | `tool_result` event with error flag and content; nothing dropped |\n    70\t| TC-2.7 *(risk: idempotency)* | Re-delivered event dedups; normal resume re-fires nothing | replay same event twice; separately, resume | re-delivery returns `skipped`/`duplicate_idempotency_key`; resume produces no historical re-fire |\n    71\t\n    72\t### `test/capture/abort.test.ts`\n    73\t\n    74\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n    75\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n    76\t| TC-2.6 | Graceful interrupt: partial content + aborted disposition; turn closes complete-but-aborted | aborted-turn corpus (`stopReason:aborted`, agent_end fires) | partial assistant content recorded; aborted disposition carried; turn closed at agent_end |\n    77\t\n    78\t> Hard-kill (no `agent_end`) is covered as a deterministic-boundary golden in `turn-derivation.test.ts`: open turn left open, tolerated as a no-op on reattach (no duplication of the recorded prefix).\n    79\t\n    80\t### `test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts`\n    81\t\n    82\t| TC | Test | Setup | Assert |\n    83\t|----|------|-------|--------|\n    84\t| TC-3.1 *(risk: source-vs-derived)* | Fork creates new thread; source receives no writes | capture a thread, fork it | new thread created; source **logical read-back** (events/messages/turns) unchanged; fork point resolved from `session_before_fork` hook (PI session tree as Epic-1 fallback) |\n    85\t| TC-3.2 | Fork seeded by replay; read-back matches source through fork point | fork at a known entry | seeded thread read-back equals source read-back through the fork point |\n   154\t### Chunk 2: Capture\n   155\t\n   156\t- **Skeleton:** `map-message.ts`, `turn-accumulator.ts`, `idempotency.ts` (`NotImplementedError`); `converter.ts` (structured result).\n   157\t- **Red:** TC-2.1–2.9 + idempotency + atomicity risk tests, failing. Turn-derivation goldens (worked example, abort, hard-kill) written here.\n   158\t- **Green:** mapping fan-out, turn accumulation, runtime-change capture (model/thinking → runtime_note), key construction, batch flush with failure isolation.\n   159\t- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 11 tests pass. Highest-risk chunk — turn derivation and dedup are the load-bearing mechanics.\n   160\t\n   161\t### Chunk 3: Verification\n   162\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
